     "summaryEn": "The manufacturer must state the limits of accuracy when applicable (§1). Numerically expressed values must be in commonly accepted, standardised units of measurement wherever possible and understood by users (§2). Safety, user familiarity and established clinical practice may justify other recognised units, although global convergence on internationally standardised units is generally supported (§3).",
